					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/movingcitizen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6416381); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6416381&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606398197" alt="MovingCitizen" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6416381)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/movingcitizen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6416381); return false;" >MovingCitizen</a></span> <span class="odate time_1594830279 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Jul 2020 16:24</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4720429">
									

<p>I have to agree with this sentiment in full, with an extra helping of praising how well the story was written, even if the pickle remains depressed and moody. Judging by the author's post above, I believe that is the point. I have only minor quibbles beyond what DrLevy posted and my own personal question of &quot;Why you so good at making me feel so sad??&quot;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I feel that there isn't any mystery left in this story. In you're very successful effort to write a &quot;dark and depressing tale&#8230;&quot; you gave us all the information we can reasonably expect about the object, it's crew, and even its &quot;cargo.&quot; You could point to the allusions to a war that never happened as being the main mystery, but as DrLevy succinctly put it, that isn't enough were the focus of the story lies, so the reader can easily forget or simply not care enough about it. I also feel like exploring some aspect of the trans-dimensional nature of the sub would have been appropriate, as the Foundation would probably want to be as clear as possible as to possible origins.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

