			<div class="content" id="post-content-4747595">
									

<p>The intense horror setting in as you, the reader, realize that all this work and effort was a lie and all those people were going to die anyway is palpable.</p>
<p>Though my natural inclination is to want to know more, about the war, about how the sub transferred into the foundation’s universe&#8230; I completely appreciate why that isn’t explored here. In fact, I quite love the unsettling dread the story produces in context of a world I know very little about&#8230; leaving me with intense sadness at knowing a world died and we know just enough about it to know how it differed from ours, and nothing more.</p>
<p>+1</p>

